<title>USA: FTC OK's NGC NGL plant stake sale to Koch.</title>
<headline>FTC OK's NGC NGL plant stake sale to Koch.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Federal Trade Commission Tuesday approved NGC Corp's plan to sell its 80 percent interest in the Mont Belvieu I natural gas liquids fractionation plant to Koch Hydrocarbon Co, a division of Koch Industries, Inc.</p>
<p>The sale was required under a December 1996 consent order to help clear NGC's purchase of Chevron Corp's Warren natural gas liquids plant in Mont Belvieu, Texas.</p>
<p>The FTC had charged that without the divestiture, NGC's acquisiton of natural gas assets from Chevron would have stifled competition by leaving only two operators at the key natural gas liquids hub.</p>
</text>
